\par\plain {\f3\fs24\b0\i1 \hich\f3 \emdash \loch\f3 }
\par\plain \f3\fs24\b0\i1
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Every artist who has ever tried to capture the beauty of nature has failed. The problem is always the same: art is seduction. It distracts its audience from what is really there to focus on what the artist wants them to see.}
\par\plain \f3\fs24\b0\i1
\par\plain \f3\fs24\b0\i1
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 By the age of ten, Mandrameen could paint a portrait in oils that rivaled the old Jeketian masters. By the age of twenty, a psychedelic plant called a burgeon had reduced him to a portrait of addiction. His deliberate self-destruction attracts a feral witch who seeks an empty vessel for her god.}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 And as comes evil, so comes good\hich\f2 \emdash \loch\f2 Pel kills Mandrameen, but he resurrected by the witch Elrahet. Now he }
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 But Mandri was not brought back from the dead without conditions. He has been bonded to a living weapon of tremendous power which Elrahet and her bandit troupe have stolen from the Hrkan Lords. This weapon is a fleshcrafted youth named Obo, and if Mandri could only focus, he\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92d be able to have Obo shoot divine flames from his mouth.  The choice of Mandri as Minder may be motivated by more than mere chance, there are deeper threads of fate at play. Mandri has to }
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 These bandits are hunted, for they have amongst them a prisoner kidnapped from imperial power, a fleshcrafted being who can spit golden fire from his mouth. It is the bandit\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92s goal to use Obo to destroy the Amalgamete.}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Together, Mandrameen and Obo struggle alongside these bandits who they do not trust inside of a desert that is squeezed dry by imperialistic might. Cannibalistic tribes lurk in forgotten temples. Demons are hiding in the ground. Uncertain loyalties frame their every move, and worse, everyone Mandrameen meets wants to tell him who he is, and what he\loch\af2\hich\af2\dbch\af2\uc1\u8217\'92s meant for. In the end, he must decide between a budding friendship, incredible sacrifice, and the divine purpose written down for him when the world was made.}
\par\plain \f2\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f2\fs24\b0\i0 Bio: I graduated from Ringling College of Art and Design in 2013, and previously worked in the video game industry as a generalist (painting/sculpting/programming/design). I left the industry to pursue personal projects. Invincible Dread is one of these.}
